      "content": "Comprehension of “unaided memory” in the context of an NDA typically indicates that any retention of knowledge or \"Residuals\" that are not explicitly in tangible form - like documents, recordings, or codified data - might be allowed, particularly if they involve personal recollection and could not be detailed without infringing upon intangible memory. However, if you're at risk of legal action owing to re-implementing something you recall from your work experience, it's prudent to seek further clarification. Contracts can be interpreted differently depending on jurisdiction and industry norms, so direct consultation with an attorney familiar with NDAs and intellectual property law in the tech field would provide a definitive boundary to ensure your skills don't infringe upon the agreement. They might suggest seeking an amendment to the NDA to explicitly define the extent of permissible application of your skills obtained during your tenure with the company.",
